docker compose up --build --remove-orphans

Pro-Tip: The "Orphan" Problem
If you renamed your service inside the docker-compose.yaml file (not just the package name), you should run:
bash

docker compose up --build --remove-orphans

Use code with caution.
This Removes Containers for services that are no longer defined in your compose file, keeping your environment clean.
Did you change the service name inside your docker-compose.yaml as well, or just the package.json?

