docker compose up -d --force-recreate sniper_app

docker compose up -d --force-recreate sniper_app for what this comment mean?

docker compose up -d --force-recreate sniper_app means:

up: start the service
-d: run in background
--force-recreate: destroy and create a new container even if config/image didn’t change
sniper_app: apply only to that service
Why use it here:

Environment variable changes (SECRET_SHOP_API_BASE_URL) are applied only when container is recreated.
A normal restart may keep old env in some workflows.
So this command ensures sniper_app gets the latest env values.

